On 26 Feb., 15:18, purple arcanist <ejg_...@yahoo.com> wrote:
> I would like some help with my wizard. =A0How do I survive in the early
> game? =A0Once, I survived, but that is because I started with a ring of
> regeneration and a ring of slow digestion. =A0Should I just not get
> within melee range (that is hard), use Elbereth, or what?

Yes and yes. Before you're meleeing zap your attack spells
and throw missiles. Use Elbereth in time to increase your
chance to write it correctly and keep the critters at distance.
Repeat procedure with ranged attacks. Remember to pray
in extreem cases if you're very low on HP's and can't escape
(but don't do that too often; you can just pray once for some
period of time). And remember to flee in time if you have a
strong feeling that you cannot kill the critters. Last but not
least, let your pet help you taking out the monsters. A pet
in between your character and an attacker is a good barrier.

>
> How do I get that early wish, so I can get the Staff of Ascaliptus(sp,
> the healer quest artifact)? =A0That would really help. =A0I would also
> want the PYEC.(magic marker recharge time!)

If you could wish for what you like whenever you like without
risk it would be quite boring, don't you agree? Getting wishes
early is risky, mostly. Blessed smoky potions may give you
a wish. Sitting on a throne as well. If you want to waste some
rare blessed magic lamp you have a chance to get a wish.
(And, no, I won't tell you about fountains; chances are much
higher that you get killed there than getting a wish. ;-)

